{
  "tema": 7054,
  "slug": "sentir-sentirse",
  "titulo": "Sentir vs sentirse (to feel)",
  "subtitulo": "Me siento cansado. Siento frío.",
  "foto": "t01.jpg",
  "regla": "Sentirse + adjective or adverb says how you feel (me siento bien, se siente sola). Sentir + noun says what you feel (siento frío, siento un dolor). Lo siento = I'm sorry.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Both mean _to feel_, but they're built differently."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Form",
            "Followed by",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "sentirse",
              "adjective or adverb (how you feel)",
              "Me siento cansado."
            ],
            [
              "sentir",
              "noun (what you feel)",
              "Siento frío."
            ],
            [
              "sentir que",
              "a sentence (to feel that)",
              "Siento que va a llover."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With **sentirse**, the adjective agrees with the person: **ella se siente cansada**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Both change **e > ie**, except nosotros:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "sentir",
            "sentirse"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "siento",
              "me siento"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "sientes",
              "te sientes"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "siente",
              "se siente"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros/as",
              "sentimos",
              "nos sentimos"
            ],
            [
              "ellos, ellas, ustedes",
              "sienten",
              "se sienten"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Lo siento** = _I'm sorry_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **sentirse** is looking in the mirror (how am I?); **sentir** is reaching out to touch something (what's out there?)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Hoy ==me siento== muy bien.",
              "en": "I feel really good today."
            },
            {
              "es": "Después del entrenamiento ==me siento== cansado pero feliz.",
              "en": "After training I feel tired but happy."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Cómo ==te sientes==?",
              "en": "How do you feel?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi abuela ==se siente== sola.",
              "en": "My grandma feels lonely."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Siento== mucho frío en los pies.",
              "en": "My feet feel really cold."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Siento== un dolor en la rodilla.",
              "en": "I feel a pain in my knee."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Siento que== va a llover.",
              "en": "I feel like it's going to rain."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Lo siento==, no puedo ir.",
              "en": "I'm sorry, I can't go."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
